    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a high-upside strategy centered on capitalizing against softer pitching rotations. Our strongest play is **Josh Naylor** (77.80), who benefits from a favorable environment against Trevor Rogers. With a strong base projection buoyed by a +16% park factor, an additional +6% for hitting in the #3 slot, and a helpful wind, **Naylor** is our anchor for power production. Right behind him, **James Wood** (77.08) is an elite start against Adrian Houser. Despite a slight negative park adjustment, **Wood**\u2019s elite xwOBA (0.404) and the extra boost from hitting leadoff make him a cornerstone of the lineup, particularly with the wind blowing out adding a margin of safety to his home run potential.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Travis Bazzana** (57.55). While his profile suggests a solid floor, the daunting task of facing Gerrit Cole\u2014even with a 4.54 xERA\u2014pushed him just behind the production floor set by **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Brice Turang**. **Cole Young** (63.25) remains a priority start despite his modest base, as his leadoff status and the extreme park advantage against the left-handed Rogers make him too valuable to sit in a week where we are aggressively hunting for R and SB. We are also keeping a close eye on the volatile matchups for **Dalton Rushing** (40.29), who draws a difficult assignment in Paul Skenes; while he is barely clearing our threshold for starting, his defensive reliability keeps him in the mix as we monitor the final lineup postings.\n\nWe remain vigilant regarding our secondary hitters, as **Henry Bolte** (60.33) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (63.66) are projected to face Robert Gasser. The favorable matchup against Gasser\u2019s 5.35 xERA provides a cushion, though **Bolte**\u2019s position in the #7 spot lowers his run-scoring ceiling. Overall, our lineup is optimized for maximum exposure against Gasser and Rogers while carefully navigating the tougher arms like Skenes and Eovaldi. No major weather concerns have been flagged, but with several players still listed as \"Lineup Pending,\" we are ready to swap **Zach McKinstry** into the utility spot if our primary options are scratched or face last-minute adjustments.",
